;; May these artifacts be booted?
;;
;; Every link from the release manifest down was checked -- the manifest binds
;; the anchors artifact's digest, the document's pins are validated, the peer's
;; key is measured against them -- and the thing the hosted machine actually
;; boots was not checked at all (ADR-0048's remaining gap). This is that check.
[{:db/id -1
  :aiueos.boot/id :aiueos/default-boot-admission
  :aiueos.boot/source-files ["src/grant/boot_admission.cljk"]
  :aiueos.boot/composes ["src/grant/publisher.cljk" "src/grant/ota.cljk"]
  :aiueos.boot/enforced-by ["src/aiueos/vm.cljk"]
  :aiueos.boot/required-kinds #{:kernel :initramfs}
  :aiueos.boot/decision-shapes #{:grant :deny}
  :aiueos.boot/deny-reasons #{:no-release :kind-not-named :artifact-unmeasured
                              :artifact-digest-mismatch}
  :aiueos.boot/reasons-pass-through
  "aiueos.publisher reasons are returned unchanged"
  :aiueos.boot/checks :authenticity-not-recency
  :aiueos.boot/checks-note
  "No :installed-sequence is passed, so the monotonic check does not run.
   Booting an older release is allowed on purpose: a device that cannot boot an
   earlier image cannot be recovered, and anti-rollback belongs in the update
   path where there is a stored sequence and a running machine."
  :aiueos.boot/verified-artifacts :only-the-ones-the-launcher-boots
  :aiueos.boot/verified-artifacts-note
  "A manifest names more than a launcher touches. The anchors artifact lives
   inside the initramfs, so the initramfs digest already covers it; re-hashing
   it here would mean opening the image to check bytes the guest checks anyway,
   while presenting one measurement as two."
  :aiueos.boot/no-release :recorded-as-unverified
  :aiueos.boot/assurance-gaps
  ["This is not measured boot. The check runs on the host, in the launcher, so
    it is worth exactly as much as the host is; a compromised host verifies
    whatever it likes. The bare-metal profile answers this with firmware, the
    hosted profile cannot."
   "A launch with no :release proceeds, recording :aiueos.boot/verified? false.
    Refusing outright would break every local workflow that boots what it just
    built. No deployment profile yet requires verification, so nothing turns
    that record into a rule."
   "Signature verification is the provider's: :signatures carries a per-key
    :verified? the launcher did not compute here."
   "The bare-metal profile does not use this path at all -- os/aiueos boots
    through firmware, and its release image is verified by
    verify-release-signature.py outside this namespace."]}]
